<title>UK: Tempest survey of best funds, brokers for Latam.</title>
<headline>Tempest survey of best funds, brokers for Latam.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following are the rankings of and key findings from a Reuters-sponsored survey of fund managers, brokers and companies focused on Latin American markets and conducted over three months by Tempest Consultants. The survey was conducted among over 840 fund managers and buy-side analysts, over 230 national and international brokers and some 1,700 brokers' analysts.</p>
<p>Fund managers' rankings of the best broker research and service for Latin America:</p>
<p>1. Banco Santander de Negocios</p>
<p>2. Merrill Lynch</p>
<p>3. Salomon Brothers</p>
<p>4. J.P. Morgan</p>
<p>5. Garantia</p>
<p>Funds' ratings of best broker execution ability :</p>
<p>1. Banco Santander de Negocios</p>
<p>2. Merrill Lynch</p>
<p>3. Garantia</p>
<p>4. J.P. Morgan</p>
<p>5. Bear Stearns &amp; Co Inc</p>
<p>Funds' perceptions of best broker skills :</p>
<p>Best written research:</p>
<p>1. Garantia </p>
<p>2.Salomon Brothers</p>
<p>3.Banco Santander de Negocios</p>
<p>Best analyst telephone calls:</p>
<p>1.Banco Santander de Negocios</p>
<p>2.Merrill Lynch  </p>
<p>3.Salomon Brothers</p>
<p>Best analyst visits: </p>
<p>1.Banco Santander de Negocios</p>
<p>2.Merrill Lynch  </p>
<p>3.Garantia</p>
<p>Best sales skills: </p>
<p>1.Banco Santander de Negocios</p>
<p>2.Garantia  </p>
<p>3.Salomon Brothers</p>
<p>Funds' perception of broker research priorities:</p>
<p>Servicing institutional clients:</p>
<p>1. Caspian Securities Ltd</p>
<p>2. Banco Santander de Negocios</p>
<p>3. Robert Fleming Securities</p>
<p>4. LatInvest</p>
<p>5. Salomon Brothers</p>
<p>Proprietary Trading:</p>
<p>1. Bear Stearns &amp; Co</p>
<p>2. ING Barings</p>
<p>3. Garantia</p>
<p>4. LatInvest</p>
<p>5. Robert Fleming Securities</p>
<p>Corporate Finance</p>
<p>1. J.P. Morgan</p>
<p>2. Merrill Lynch</p>
<p>3. Salomon Brothers</p>
<p>4. Garantia</p>
<p>5. Bear Stearns &amp; Co Inc</p>
<p>The average number of company visits conducted by fund managers focused on Latin America last year was 89. Most preferred to meet CEOs and finance directors rather than investor relations or public relations officials.</p>
<p>Some 64.80 percent of funds polled said they intend to increase the number of visits next year, 35.20 percent said they would do no more and none expected to decrease the number of visits.</p>
<p>The ranking by finance directors of the top individual fund managers for Latin America:</p>
<p>1. Alex Benasuli, Soros Global Research</p>
<p>2. Lisa Thompson, Capital International</p>
<p>3. Patti Satterthwaite, Fidelity Investments</p>
<p>4. Victor Kohn, Capital International</p>
<p>5. Matthew Thorrey, Fidelity Investments</p>
<p>6. Meg Reynolds, Fidelity Investments</p>
<p>7. Bill Nord, Marvin Palmer &amp; Associates</p>
<p>8. J Mark Mobius, Templeton Investment Management</p>
<p>9. Andy Skov, Morgan Stanley Asset Management</p>
<p>10.Oscar Castro, Montgomery Asset Management</p>
<p>The ranking by finance directors of the top 10 fund management groups for Latin America</p>
<p>1. Fidelity Investments</p>
<p>2. Capital International</p>
<p>3. Morgan Stanley Asset Management</p>
<p>4. Merrill Lynch Asset Management</p>
<p>5. Scudder, Stevens &amp; Clark Inc</p>
<p>6. Soros Global Research</p>
<p>7. Templeton Investment Management</p>
<p>8. Montgomery Asset Management</p>
<p>9. Kleinwort Benson Investment Management</p>
<p>10.Marvin Palmer &amp; Associates</p>
<p>The ranking by finance directors of broker research for Latin America:</p>
<p>Best written research: 1.J.P. Morgan  2.Garantia  3. Merrill Lynch</p>
<p>Best use of time: </p>
<p>1.J.P. Morgan  </p>
<p>2.Merrill Lynch  </p>
<p>3.Garantia</p>
<p>Depth of knowledge:  </p>
<p>1.J.P. Morgan  </p>
<p>2.Merrill Lynch</p>
<p>3.Garantia</p>
<p>Quality of relationship:  </p>
<p>1.J.P. Morgan  </p>
<p>2.Merrill Lynch</p>
<p>3.Salomon Brothers</p>
<p>The full survey, including an explanation of methodology, is available from Tempest Consultants in London.</p>
<p>-- Caroline Allen, London newsroom +44 171 542 6414</p>
